    "q-92929": {
      "dom_id": "step-q92929",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Determine the $y$-intercept of $y={(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2x}+1.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2(0)}+1 \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{10})}^{0}+1 \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
