    "q-40556": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40556",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following values ​are possible outputs of $f(x)=-5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1}+3?$\n\nI. $-3$\n\nII. $2$\n\nIII. $10$",
      "worked_solution": "The range of ${(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}>0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-5$ and then adding $3,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1} & >0 \\\\ -5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1} & <0 \\\\ -5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1}+3 & <0+3 \\\\ f(x) & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)<3.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=-3$ and $y=2$ are  outputs of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254086/assets/b220b9c53bfaa49fe9b1b1c70fb9e21d08e247f44df8716846d08fd37ac2cf11.png)\n\n  \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
