      "dom_id": "step-q92988",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=2({e}^{2x})-5.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254086/assets/fc2af8bae74f163f0dd4eae74fd90fc6c5460cae552c7e5072c83521444aea29.png)\n\nSince the function approaches the line $y=-5$ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we conclude that the equation of the horizontal asymptote is $y=-5.$",
