      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Suppose that $f(x)=2({3}^{x})-1.$ Given that $f(x)\\to a$ as $x\\to \\infty ,$ then $a=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254086/assets/16222c983e8b7f961b76fedcf9cc3bb45fdde7768fd0b272dc9367605dfce1cf.png)\n\nSince the function grows without bound as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(x)\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\infty .$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
