      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)={e}^{1-x}-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254086/assets/3ee68df58de38e90368214f98aa22ecc1be79dec2e38f2ae7dd41b6900077b28.png)\n\nSince the function approaches the line $y=-3$ as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we conclude that the equation of the horizontal asymptote is $y=-3.$",
