      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=2({e}^{5x+3})-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254086/assets/fc106ec93af058dd4a5416cd4fcb5740d2613151a0e31672658771c250f61bfe.png)\n\nSince the function approaches the line $y=-1$ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we conclude that the equation of the horizontal asymptote is $y=-1.$",
